unibutton.gadget/--datasheet--               unibutton.gadget/--datasheet--

    NAME
        unibutton.gadget -- Unicode/Emoji push-button gadget

    SUPERCLASS
        gadgetclass

    REQUIRES
        utf8rastport.library, bevel.image

    DESCRIPTION
        UniButton is a BOOPSI gadget class that provides a push-button
        widget whose label is rendered by utf8rastport.library using a
        FreeType font.  Unlike the system button.gadget (which draws
        labels with the Amiga Text() call), UniButton can display full
        Unicode text and colour Emoji in button labels.

        The normal, selected, and disabled visual states are pre-rendered
        into off-screen BitMaps cached inside the gadget.  Responding to
        mouse clicks (which occurs in input.device context) therefore only
        needs a safe BltBitMapRastPort and does not call FreeType at
        interrupt time.

        A URPDrawContext (font and glyph cache) can be shared between
        multiple UniButton instances via UBT_URPDrawContext, exactly as
        UTED_URPDrawContext works in UniTextEditor.  Sharing one context
        keeps all buttons in a window using the same cached glyphs.

    METHODS
        OM_NEW       -- Initialise gadget; load font; pre-render states.
        OM_SET       -- Apply attribute tags; re-render states as needed.
        OM_GET       -- Return attribute values.
        OM_DISPOSE   -- Free cached bitmaps and release draw context.
        GM_RENDER    -- Blit the appropriate pre-rendered state bitmap.
        GM_HITTEST   -- Standard gadget hit test.
        GM_GOACTIVE  -- Activate gadget (highlight selected state).
        GM_HANDLEINPUT -- Track release inside/outside gadget bounds.
        GM_GOINACTIVE -- Deactivate; send UBTN_Pressed if released inside.
        GM_DOMAIN    -- Return GDOMAIN_MINIMUM and GDOMAIN_MAXIMUM dimensions.

    ATTRIBUTES
        -- Font configuration --

        UniButton renders its label through a font fallback chain managed
        by utf8rastport.library, exactly as UniTextEditor does.  The chain
        is walked in order for every codepoint: the first font that contains
        a glyph for that codepoint is used.

        Fonts must be added in priority order:
          1. Primary font   -- the preferred typeface for label text.
          2. Fallback fonts -- cover codepoints absent from earlier fonts.
          3. Emoji font     -- a colour bitmap font (e.g. NotoColorEmoji)
                              added last so ordinary text takes priority.

        This allows a button label such as "Save 💾" or "OK ✔" to render
        both the text glyphs and the Emoji glyph from the same chain
        without any application-level character routing.

        A complete font configuration -- or a reconfiguration at any time
        -- can be sent in a single SetGadgetAttrs() call:

          1. UBT_FlushFonts   -- discard the current chain and glyph cache.
          2. UBT_PointSize    -- set the size for subsequent AddFont calls.
          3. UBT_AddFont      -- primary font (repeat for each fallback and
             UBT_AddFont         the Emoji font).
             ...

        Example -- set up or reconfigure at runtime:

          SetGadgetAttrs(btnGadget, window, NULL,
              UBT_FlushFonts,  TRUE,
              UBT_PointSize,   14,
              UBT_AddFont,     "FONTS:DejaVuSans.ttf",
              UBT_AddFont,     "FONTS:NotoColorEmoji.ttf",
              TAG_END);

        UBT_PointSize  (TAG_USER|0x7301)  [IS]  (ULONG)
            Font point size in screen pixels.  Default: 14.

        UBT_URPPrefs  (TAG_USER|0x7302)  [IS]  (ULONG)
            URP_PREF_* flags forwarded to the draw context.
            Default: URP_PREF_ANTIALIAS | URP_PREF_CLUTMODE_NOMASK |
                     URP_PREF_HIGHFILTERING.

        UBT_FontFlags  (TAG_USER|0x7306)  [IS]  (ULONG)
            Flags stored for subsequent UBT_AddFont calls.  Default: 0.

        UBT_AddFont  (TAG_USER|0x7307)  [IS]  (STRPTR)
            Load one font file and append it to the end of the fallback
            chain, using the current UBT_PointSize and UBT_FontFlags.
            Include this tag multiple times in one SetGadgetAttrs() call
            to build the full chain in a single operation.
            The path string is not copied by the gadget.

        UBT_FlushFonts  (TAG_USER|0x7308)  [IS]
            Flush all fonts and the glyph cache.  Place this tag before
            UBT_PointSize and UBT_AddFont to perform a full
            reconfiguration in one SetGadgetAttrs() call.

        UBT_URPDrawContext  (TAG_USER|0x730B)  [ISG]  (struct URPDrawContext *)
            Shared draw context.  The gadget calls URPDC_Retain() on
            the supplied pointer.  Retrieve via OM_GET to share with a
            second UniButton instance.

        -- Colours --

        UBT_TextPen  (TAG_USER|0x7303)  [IS]  (ULONG)
            Intuition pen for the text foreground.  Default: 1.

        UBT_BgPen  (TAG_USER|0x7304)  [IS]  (ULONG)
            Intuition pen for the button background (normal state).
            Default: 0.

        UBT_SelBgPen  (TAG_USER|0x7305)  [IS]  (ULONG)
            Intuition pen for the button background in the selected
            (pressed) state.  Default: FILLPEN from DrawInfo (pen 3).

        -- Appearance --

        UBT_BevelStyle  (TAG_USER|0x7309)  [IG]  (ULONG)
            Bevel style from bevel.h (BVS_* constants).
            Default: BVS_BUTTON.  May only be set at OM_NEW.

        UBT_Transparent  (TAG_USER|0x730A)  [IS]  (BOOL)
            When TRUE, background fill is skipped; the button appears
            transparent.  Default: FALSE.

        -- Margins --
            All margins are measured in pixels INSIDE the bevel frame.
            The bevel thickness is added automatically on top.

        UBT_LeftMargin    (TAG_USER|0x730C)  [ISG]  (ULONG)  Default: 4.
        UBT_RightMargin   (TAG_USER|0x730D)  [ISG]  (ULONG)  Default: 4.
        UBT_TopMargin     (TAG_USER|0x730E)  [ISG]  (ULONG)  Default: 2.
        UBT_BottomMargin  (TAG_USER|0x730F)  [ISG]  (ULONG)  Default: 2.

        -- Standard gadget attributes (inherited) --

        GA_Text  (STRPTR)
            NUL-terminated label string for the button.  Rendered with
            the loaded FreeType font.

        GA_ID  (WORD)
            Unique gadget identifier.  Returned as the value of
            UBTN_Pressed when the button is activated.

        GA_Disabled  (BOOL)
            When TRUE, the button ignores activation attempts and renders
            in a ghosted disabled state.

    NOTIFICATIONS
        Sent via OM_NOTIFY when the button is released with the pointer
        still over the gadget.  Connect with ICA_TARGET / ICA_MAP.

        UBTN_Pressed  (TAG_USER|0x73C1)
            Button activated.  Value = GA_ID of the button.

    SEE ALSO
        utf8rastport.library/--datasheet--,
        unitexteditor_gc/--datasheet--,
        unibutton.gadget/UNIBUTTON_GetClass

unibutton.gadget/UNIBUTTON_GetClass         unibutton.gadget/UNIBUTTON_GetClass

    NAME
        UNIBUTTON_GetClass -- obtain the UniButton gadget class pointer

    SYNOPSIS
        class = UNIBUTTON_GetClass();
        D0

        Class *UNIBUTTON_GetClass(VOID);

    FUNCTION
        Returns the pointer to the UniButton BOOPSI gadget class for
        use with NewObject().  The class is set up when the library is
        opened; this function always returns a valid pointer provided
        that unibutton.gadget opened successfully.

        The typical usage sequence is:

            UniButtonBase = OpenLibrary("gadgets/unibutton.gadget", 1);
            if (!UniButtonBase) { /* error */ }
            btn = NewObject(UNIBUTTON_GetClass(), NULL,
                            GA_Text,        "Click Me 😀",
                            GA_ID,          MY_BTN_ID,
                            GA_RelVerify,   TRUE,
                            UBT_PointSize,  14,
                            UBT_AddFont,    "FONTS:MyFont.ttf",
                            TAG_END);

        The gadget notifies via UBTN_Pressed when the button is clicked.

    INPUTS
        None.

    RESULT
        class -- pointer to the UniButton Class structure.

    SEE ALSO
        unibutton.gadget/--datasheet--,
        utf8rastport.library/URPDC_Create
